sn35.33:1.16 starts: The mind … Whatever feeling arises
sn35.33:1.17 starts: Whatever feeling arises with mind-contact as condition
sn45.18:2.2 starts: What now, friend, is the unholy life?”
sn56.35:2.2 starts: For what reason?
sn56.35:2.3 starts: Because this saṁsara is without discoverable beginning;
mn140:4.3 starts: and the venerable Pukkusāti also spent most
mn140:10.6 starts: On tasting a flavour with the tongue…
mn140:10.7 starts: On touching a tangible with the body…
mn140:10.8 starts: On cognizing a mind-object with the mind,
mn140:18.4 starts: Whatever internally, belonging to oneself, is space,
mn140:18.5 starts: the holes of the ears, the nostrils,
mn140:21.6 starts: …to the base of nothingness…
mn140:21.8 starts: to the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception and to develop
mn140:22.6 starts: to the base of nothingness…to the base
mn140:22.8 starts: to the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception and to develop
mn140:35.2 starts: Then, while the venerable Pukkusāti was searching
